Track 1: The Shuttle Swallows the Weft
- Story & Context: During the record winter of 1999 at the St. Jude priory sub-cellar, novice archivist Jonas Kroll attempted to patch an elder monk's recurring dream of drowning into an uncalibrated Doepfer oscillator, accidentally initiating an infinite feedback loop that spiked into an unbearable, screaming pitch riser. As the terrified choir pounded on the locked oak doors, visiting fabricator Maren Sölder rammed an aluminum-neck baritone guitar into a wall of rusted tube preamps, slamming out a monstrous Drop-F downbeat that shattered three leaded-glass transom windows. Kroll leaned over the smoking chassis, howling "The spool won't stop until the bone turns clean!" into a broadcast microphone while the tape machines ran red with voltage distortion. That chaotic ten-minute bootleg recording became the legendary blueprint for the entire regional movement.
