Track 2: Father Alipius, Did the Patch Hold?
- Story & Context: Exiled from the priory and holed up in a freezing Klagenfurt freight warehouse smelling of diesel and damp sheep fleece, Prior Alipius broke his solemn seven-year silence to record this confession through an overdriven guitar pickup pressed against his larynx. He revealed that the monastery's celebrated dream patches were not communion with angels, but desperate transcriptions of an auditory parasite that hummed in ascending pitch whenever the novices closed their eyes. Greta Vane framed his trembling confession against a sledgehammer industrial tempo and a nauseating, tape-slurred sine riser, whispering the chorus: "You stitched your faith to iron teeth and called it grace." When the track reached its suffocating crescendo, Alipius collapsed onto the cold concrete, leaving his abandoned patch cables to hiss against the amplifier ground.
