Track 3: Phase-Inverted Selvedge
- Story & Context: In the aftermath of the scene's dissolution, the trio staged a single, unannounced performance inside the cavernous limestone amphitheater of the Black Quarry near Eisenkappel. Armed with two daisy-chained modular rigs and three bass stacks pushed to their thermal limits, the band triggered a continuously ascending, ten-minute Shepard-riser that physically vibrated chalk dust from the quarry walls onto the silent crowd below. When the ascending tone breached human hearing into pure ultrasonic pressure, Sölder severed the guitar cables with a pair of shears, leaving Vane to cast the final words into the ringing silence: "Every knot we tied tore the cloth in two." By dawn, nothing remained at the site except piles of white mineral dust, severed cords, and the persistent phantom drone still reported by local hikers today.
